# ── Where the Vokve API lives ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The admin panel reads `${VOKVE_API_URL}/admin/*`, server-side only. Include
# the version prefix.
VOKVE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000/v1

# The zone every date on the dashboard is bucketed in, sent to the API as
# `X-Vokve-Timezone`. A "day" in the panel is then the day you are living in
# rather than UTC's.
VOKVE_ADMIN_TIMEZONE=Asia/Kolkata

# ── The operator's key ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Normally you do not set this: you paste the key into the sign-in page and it
# is kept in an httpOnly cookie for twelve hours.
#
# Set it here only for local development, where it saves signing in on every
# restart. It is **ignored when NODE_ENV=production** — on a deployed panel,
# anybody who could reach the URL would already be an operator.
#
# It must be the same value as ADMIN_API_KEY on vokve-backend.
# VOKVE_ADMIN_API_KEY=change-me-to-a-long-random-admin-key

# ── Production hardening (read by src/proxy.ts) ──────────────────────────────
# CANONICAL_HOST=admin.vokve.app
# ALLOWED_HOSTS=admin.vokve.app
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://admin.vokve.app
